---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const title = `About | ${SITE_TITLE}`;
const description = "who even is lazynoman?";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article>
				<span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">
					lazynoman.com — about
				</span>

				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6">who even is lazynoman?</h1>
				<p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-muted-foreground mb-12 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
					the short answer: someone who ran out of things to read. the long answer is below.
				</p>

				<hr class="my-12" />

				<div class="space-y-8">
					<p>
						okay so. at some point i hit a wall. i had read so many webnovels, so many manga chapters, watched so much anime
						that i genuinely ran out of stuff that matched my taste. not like "i can't find anything right now" — i mean i
						actually exhausted the genres i liked. that's not a brag, it's just what happens when you consume stories the
						way i do.
					</p>

					<p>
						i'm not a 30-minutes-today, 30-minutes-tomorrow type of person. when i'm into something i sit down and i go.
						full day. if a manga has finished its story in novel form, i'm reading the novel. if an anime is still airing
						but the manga is done, i'm reading the manga and probably never coming back to the anime.
						<span class="text-muted-foreground font-medium italic">(sorry not sorry.)</span> i don't rewatch. i don't reread. i just keep moving
						forward until there's nothing left.
					</p>

					<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 my-10">
						<div class="bg-muted/50 border border-border rounded-xl px-5 py-3 text-base">
							<strong class="text-foreground">130+</strong> webnovels read
						</div>
						<div class="bg-muted/50 border border-border rounded-xl px-5 py-3 text-base">
							<strong class="text-foreground">20,000+</strong> manga/manhwa chapters
						</div>
						<div class="bg-muted/50 border border-border rounded-xl px-5 py-3 text-base font-medium">
							novels &gt; manga &gt; anime
						</div>
					</div>

					<p>
						so when you've consumed that much, two things happen. one — you develop opinions. strong ones. you know what
						actually works in a story and what's just filler dressed up in pretty art. two — you start wanting to tell
						other people what's worth their time so they don't have to waste it on the stuff that isn't.
					</p>

					<p>
						that's what this site is. i'm not a critic, i'm not a journalist, i'm just someone who's been deep in this
						world long enough to have a real read on it. i won't sugarcoat. if something is mid i'll say it's mid. if
						something actually wrecked me in the best way i'll tell you that too.
					</p>

					<hr class="my-12" />

					<section>
						<h3 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-muted-foreground mb-6">what i actually like</h3>
						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-12">
							{['fantasy', 'isekai (when done right)', 'cultivation novels', 'slow-burn with payoff', 'deep world-building', 'manhwa', 'animation movies'].map(tag => (
								<span class="text-sm rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 bg-primary/10 text-primary border border-primary/20 font-medium">{tag}</span>
							))}
						</div>
					</section>

					<section>
						<h3 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-muted-foreground mb-6">what i can't stand</h3>
						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-12">
							{['incomplete adaptations', 'filler that goes nowhere', 'anime that stops before the good part', 'rewatching/rereading'].map(tag => (
								<span class="text-sm rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 bg-destructive/10 text-destructive border border-destructive/20 font-medium">{tag}</span>
							))}
						</div>
					</section>

					<div class="bg-muted/30 border border-border rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 mb-12 relative overflow-hidden group">
						<div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-primary/5 rounded-full -mr-16 -mt-16 transition-transform group-hover:scale-110"></div>
						<h3 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-muted-foreground mb-4">the big dream</h3>
						<p class="text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed m-0 text-foreground/90">
							one day i want to build a proper tracking platform — something where you can log every anime, manga, novel,
							and game in one place and actually see it all together. anilist is great but it doesn't cover everything.
							that's a project for later. for now this site is where i put my thoughts while i figure out how to build
							that thing.
						</p>
					</div>

					<p class="text-xl">
						if you're also someone who ran out of good things to read and you're desperately hunting for the next story
						that won't disappoint you — you're in the right place. welcome.
					</p>

					<p class="text-muted-foreground mt-16 flex items-center gap-2">
						— <span class="font-bold text-foreground text-lg tracking-tight">lazynoman</span>
					</p>
				</div>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>